{
  "slug": "js_debugging_async",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 111,
  "url": "/js/js_debugging_async.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Debugging Async",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Debugging Async"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Debugging Async Code"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Async bugs are the hardest bugs for beginners."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The code looks correct, but nothing seems to happen."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Why Async Code Is Hard to Debug"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Async code runs later."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This makes errors feel invisible."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Common beginner problems include missing data and silent failures."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Async code does not run top to bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It runs when something finishes."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Debugging fetch()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The fetch() function is asynchronous."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It does not return data immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "fetch(\"data.json\")\n\n.then(response => response.json())\n\n.then(data => console.log(data));",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If nothing appears, check the console first."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Always log the response before using the data."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "fetch(\"data.json\")\n\n.then(response => {\n\n  console.log(response);\n\n  return response.json();\n\n})\n\n.then(data => console.log(data));",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Check the Network Tab"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Async bugs are often network problems."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The Network tab shows if a request failed."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Check the request status.",
        "Check the file path.",
        "Check if the server returned an error."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Debugging async and await"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "async and await make async code easier to read."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "They are still asynchronous."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "async function loadData() {\n\n  let response = await fetch(\"data.json\");\n\n  let data = await response.json();\n\n  console.log(data);\n\n}\n\nloadData();",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can set breakpoints on await lines."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Step through async code the same way as normal code."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Handling Async Errors"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Async errors must be handled explicitly."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Otherwise they fail silently."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "async function loadData() {\n\n  try {\n\n    let response = await fetch(\"wrong.json\");\n\n    let data = await response.json();\n\n    console.log(data);\n\n  } catch (error) {\n\n    console.error(error);\n\n  }\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Errors inside async functions must be caught."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Promises That Never Resolve"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Sometimes async code never finishes."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This usually means a missing return."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "function getData() {\n\n  fetch(\"data.json\")\n\n  .then(response => response.json());\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The promise result is never returned."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Always return promises when chaining."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Debugging Checklist for Async Code"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Check the console for errors.",
        "Check the Network tab.",
        "Log responses before using them.",
        "Use try...catch with async functions.",
        "Set breakpoints on await lines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "You Finished the Debugging Chapters"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You now know how to debug JavaScript step by step."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This skill separates beginners from real developers."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Debugging is not a talent."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It is a habit."
    }
  ]
}
